Package: recurcast
Type: Package
Title: Coherent Forecasts for Recurrent and Terminal Events
Version: 0.10.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Sunday A.", "Adetunji", email = "adetunjs@oregonstate.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Oluwatimileyin A.", "Adetunji", role = "aut"))
Description: Fits shared-frailty event-history models and computes joint-law
    forecasts of recurrence burden, terminal-event risk and restricted survival.
    Provides automatic coarsened-history integration, sparse propagation,
    finite-path and continuous-time targeted estimation, scalable finite-support
    recording-sensitivity bounds, evolving-covariate forecasts, alternative frailty
    distributions, weighted conformal calculations, and calibration diagnostics.
    Observation assumptions and numerical error bounds are retained
    in returned objects. The estimands are prognostic rather than causal.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: Rcpp, stats, utils, graphics, digest, jsonlite
LinkingTo: Rcpp
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0), survival, frailtypack, ggplot2, knitr, rmarkdown, nlme
VignetteBuilder: knitr
SystemRequirements: C++17
Config/testthat/edition: 3
NeedsCompilation: yes
